From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Myles Liu <lyx981mike@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:25:45 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] qualcommax: ipq50xx: redmi-ax3000: enable TSENS

The driver enables TSENS itself on IPQ5018 (init_tsens_v1_no_rpm), so the
"not enabled by the boot firmware" reason for keeping it off no longer
applies. Measured on the RA81 with NSS and Wi-Fi offload under full load:
48-53 C on all four zones, smooth, no bogus readings (tested first with the
critical trips demoted to hot). Keep the upstream trip points.
---
 target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts
index 1109e40..56851b4 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts
@@ -109,13 +109,14 @@
 };
 
 /*
- * TSENS is not enabled by the boot firmware on this IPQ5000 ("tsens
- * device is not enabled" with the vendor kernel) and some of its zones
- * report bogus critical temperatures, which shuts the board down early
- * in boot - before the dual-boot rollback is armed. Keep it off.
+ * TSENS: the boot firmware leaves it disabled on this IPQ5000, but the
+ * driver enables it itself (init_tsens_v1_no_rpm, no RPM on IPQ5018).
+ * Measured on an RA81 with NSS + Wi-Fi offload: 48-53 C idle to full load
+ * on all four zones, smooth (<= 2 C per 2 s), no bogus readings. Keep the
+ * upstream trips (CPU passive 100 C, critical 120 C).
  */
 &tsens {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &sleep_clk {
-- 
